{
  "name": "Tablecloth Trick · integ.life",
  "short_name": "Tablecloth Trick",
  "description": "A family table laid with a silk cloth: a tea cup, Mum's bowls, a whole braised fish, Grandma's thermos and the family heirloom. Grab the hem and flick it down. Fast enough and the cloth slides out while everything rattles and stays; too slow and the whole table rides over the edge. Six tables, each harder than the last, and a cat. A tiny cloth-physics toy, no sign-up.",
